# CLAUDE.md

This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.

## Overview
TJG（天机阁）is a modern, cross-platform Instant Messaging (IM) system. It leverages **Tauri v2** for the application container, **Vite 7** for fast frontend tooling, **Vue 3** for the user interface, and **TypeScript** for type safety. The backend logic is implemented in **Rust**.

The project supports:
- **Desktop:** Windows, macOS, Linux
- **Mobile:** Android, iOS

## Tech Stack

### Frontend
- **Framework:** Vue 3 (Composition API, `<script setup>`)
- **Language:** TypeScript
- **Build Tool:** Vite 7
- **State Management:** Pinia (with `pinia-plugin-persistedstate`)
- **Routing:** Vue Router
- **Styling:** UnoCSS, Sass/SCSS
- **UI Libraries:** Naive UI (Desktop), Vant (Mobile)
- **I18n:** vue-i18n
- **Auto Import:** `unplugin-auto-import`, `unplugin-vue-components`
- **Component Docs:** Storybook

### Backend (Rust / Tauri)
- **Core:** Tauri v2 (`tauri = "2.9.5"`)
- **Database:** SQLite via `tauri-plugin-sql` + SeaORM (`1.1.19`) with `sqlx-sqlite`
- **Async Runtime:** Tokio (`1.48.0`)
- **HTTP Client:** Reqwest (`0.12`, rustls-tls)
- **WebSocket:** tokio-tungstenite (`0.28`)
- **Audio:** Rodio (`0.21.1`)
- **Key Tauri Plugins:** log, fs, dialog, clipboard-manager, autostart, notification, updater, global-shortcut, os, shell, opener, barcode-scanner

### Matrix Protocol Integration
- **SDK:** Local `matrix-js-sdk` fork, vendored as a pinned tarball (`file:vendor/matrix-js-sdk.tgz`, locked by `meta/sdk-pin.json`)
- **Backend:** [synapse-rust](https://github.com/langkebo/synapse-rust) - Rust-based Matrix Homeserver
- **Sync:** Sliding Sync (`SlidingSync`) used for efficient room sync
- **Worker:** Matrix SDK runs in a Web Worker (`src/workers/matrixSdk.worker.ts`) to keep main thread < 50ms blocked
- **Error Handling:** Uses `throwOnError` mode - read operations throw exceptions by default
- **Extensions:** Includes synapse-rust specific manager extensions (friend relationships, widgets, voice messages)

## Development Workflow

### Prerequisites
- Node.js (v20+ recommended)
- pnpm (v10+ recommended)
- Rust (latest stable, edition 2024)
- Android Studio / Xcode (for mobile development)

### Local Development Setup
1. Clone the repository
2. Run `pnpm install` — the Matrix SDK installs from the vendored tarball `vendor/matrix-js-sdk.tgz` (pinned in `meta/sdk-pin.json`); no sibling SDK checkout is needed
3. Ensure you have access to a synapse-rust backend instance (see [synapse-rust](https://github.com/langkebo/synapse-rust))
4. Configure `VITE_HOMESERVER_URL` in `.env.local` (never commit this file)

### SDK Co-Development (optional)
Day-to-day frontend work only needs this repo plus a synapse-rust backend. The sibling `../matrix-js-sdk` checkout is required only when changing the SDK itself:
1. **synapse-rust** - Backend Matrix Homeserver (default port: 8008)
2. **matrix-js-sdk** - SDK fork (sibling directory `../matrix-js-sdk`, only needed for SDK changes)
3. **Tjg** - This frontend application

To pick up SDK changes: build the SDK (`pnpm --dir ../matrix-js-sdk build`), then run
`node scripts/pack-sdk-tarball.mjs --allow-commit-drift --apply` followed by `pnpm install`.
This refreshes `vendor/matrix-js-sdk.tgz` and `meta/sdk-pin.json` — commit both together.
`node scripts/pack-sdk-tarball.mjs --restore` temporarily switches back to `link:` mode for rapid
SDK iteration; never commit in link mode (`verify:sdk-pin` rejects it on release branches).

### Environment Variables
- `VITE_APP_NAME` - Application name
- `VITE_HOMESERVER_URL` - Matrix Homeserver URL (default: `http://localhost:8008`)
- `VITE_PC_URL` - Frontend repository URL
- `VITE_SERVICE_URL` - Backend (synapse-rust) repository URL
- `TAURI_ENV_PLATFORM` - Set by Tauri; `windows`/`darwin`/`linux` for desktop, `android`/`ios` for mobile

### Testing Strategy
- **Unit Tests:** Vitest for service layer and utilities (`src/**/__tests__/*.test.ts`)
- **E2E Tests:** Playwright for end-to-end flows (`e2e/*.spec.ts`)
- **Coverage:** Run `pnpm coverage` to generate coverage reports
- **Type Safety:** Always run `vue-tsc --noEmit` before committing
- **Storybook:** `pnpm storybook` for component visual development

### Key Commands

| Action | Command | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Install Dependencies** | `pnpm install` | Installs Node.js dependencies. |
| **Start Desktop Dev** | `pnpm tauri:dev` or `pnpm td` | Starts the Tauri development server for desktop. |
| **Build Desktop** | `pnpm tauri:build` or `pnpm tb` | Builds the production application for desktop (interactive script). |
| **Start Android Dev** | `pnpm adev` | Starts Android development (requires Android Studio). |
| **Start iOS Dev** | `pnpm idev` | Starts iOS development (requires Xcode, macOS only). |
| **Android Frontend Only (Windows)** | `pnpm adev:win` | Starts Android frontend without Tauri (Windows). |
| **iOS Frontend Only (macOS)** | `pnpm idev:mac` | Starts iOS frontend without Tauri (macOS). |
| **Commit Changes** | `pnpm commit` | Interactive git commit using Commitizen. |
| **Lint/Format** | `pnpm check` | Checks code using Biome (read-only). |
| **Fix Lint/Format** | `pnpm check:write` | Fixes code issues using Biome. |
| **Format Vue Templates** | `pnpm format:vue` | Formats Vue templates with Prettier. |
| **Format All** | `pnpm format:all` | Runs Biome + Prettier on all files. |
| **Frontend Only Dev** | `pnpm dev` | Starts Vite dev server without Tauri (browser only). |
| **Run Tests** | `pnpm test:run` | Runs unit tests with Vitest. |
| **Run Single Test** | `pnpm vitest run <path>` | Runs a specific test file (e.g. `pnpm vitest run src/services/matrix/auth/__tests__/foo.test.ts`). |
| **Test with UI** | `pnpm test:ui` | Opens Vitest UI with coverage. |
| **Test Coverage** | `pnpm coverage` | Generates test coverage report. |
| **E2E Tests** | `pnpm test:e2e` | Runs Playwright end-to-end tests. |
| **Type Check** | `vue-tsc --noEmit` | Runs TypeScript type checking. |
| **Check SDK Types** | `pnpm check:sdk-types` | Validates matrix-js-sdk type augmentations. |
| **Bundle Analysis** | `pnpm metrics:bundle` | Reports bundle size metrics. |
| **Link HuLa Skill** | `pnpm skill` | Links the custom HuLa skill for development. |
| **Storybook** | `pnpm storybook` | Starts Storybook component explorer on port 6006. |

### Directory Structure

- **`src/`**: Frontend source code.
  - **`views/`**: Page-level components (windows: `homeWindow`, `loginWindow`, `settingsWindow`, `adminWindow`, `openclaw`, etc.).
  - **`stores/domains/`**: Pinia stores organized by domain:
    - **`chat/`**: Room, message, contacts, badge, emoji, moderation, history, sync stores.
    - **`settings/`**: Config, guide, plugins, mobile, alwaysOnTop, menu stores.
    - **`user/`**: User, userStatus, userMenu, loginHistory, bot stores.
    - **`admin/`**: Admin-related stores.
    - **`widget/`**: Widget stores.
  - **`services/`**: Service layer.
    - **`matrix/`**: Matrix protocol services (organized by subdomain):
      - **`auth/`**: `MatrixAuthService`, `MatrixOidcService`, `MatrixQrLoginSdkService`, `MatrixSessionService`, `MatrixRuntimeSessionService`.
      - **`room/`**: `MatrixRoomService`, `MatrixGroupService`, `MatrixDirectMessageService`, `MatrixSpaceService`, `MatrixRoomSummaryService`, timeline, lifecycle, membership, metadata, moderation, pins, tags, state, aliases, translation services.
      - **`messaging/`**: `MatrixMessageService`, `MatrixThreadService`, `MatrixReactionService`, `MatrixTypingService`, `MatrixReceiptService`, `MatrixForwardService`, `MatrixEmojiService`, `MatrixBurnAfterReadService`, `MatrixMessageRelationService`, `MatrixMessageAdapter`.
      - **`media/`**: `MatrixMediaService`, `MatrixVoiceService`, `MatrixMultimediaService`, `MatrixVoIPService`, `MatrixLocationService`, `MatrixBeaconService`, `MatrixUrlPreviewService`.
      - **`user/`**: `MatrixProfileService`, `MatrixPresenceService`, `MatrixAccountService`, `MatrixContactService`, `MatrixDeviceService`, `MatrixUserDirectoryService`.
      - **`friends/`**: `MatrixFriendService`, `MatrixSpecialFriendService`.
      - **`notifications/`**: `MatrixNotificationService`, `MatrixPushService`, `MatrixRoomNotificationService`, `MatrixServerNotificationService`.
      - **`crypto/`**: `MatrixCryptoService`, `MatrixEncryptionService`, `MatrixKeyBackupService`, `MatrixVerificationService`, `MatrixDehydratedDeviceService`, `MatrixEncryptionContextService`, `CryptoHealthMonitor`.
      - **`sync/`**: `MatrixSyncService`, `MatrixSlidingSyncService`, `SlidingSyncReconnectManager`.
      - **`admin/`**: `MatrixAdminService`, `AdminFacadeService`, room/user/media/security/federation/retention/quota/report/notification/registration token admin services.
      - **`ai/`**: `AIService`, `ApiKeyService`, `ChatRoleService`, `ConversationService`, `ModelService`.
      - **`widget/`**: `MatrixWidgetService`.
      - **`MatrixClientService.ts`**: Core client management (connection, Sliding Sync init, manager extensions).
      - **`MatrixCacheManager.ts`**: Client-side caching layer.
      - **`MatrixEventService.ts`**: Event subscription and dispatch.
      - **`MatrixRequestDeduper.ts`**: Deduplication of in-flight requests.
      - **`MatrixSearchService.ts`**: Full-text search.
      - **`SynapseRustExtensionsService.ts`**: synapse-rust specific API extensions.
    - **`backend/`**: Backend config and HTTP client (`config.ts`, `endpoints.ts`, `types.ts`).
    - **`offline/`**: `OfflineQueueService` for queuing messages when disconnected.
    - **`performance/`**: `ChunkUploadService` for large file uploads.
    - **`openclaw/`**: `OpenClawService` - OpenAI-compatible AI gateway (streaming, reconnect).
    - **`siliconflow/`**: `SiliconFlowService` - SiliconFlow AI provider.
    - **`trendradar/`**: `TrendRadarService` - trending news/content aggregation.
    - **`ai-provider.ts`**: Unified AI provider abstraction (`AIProviderType`: `openclaw` | `trendradar` | `hula`).
  - **`composables/`**: Vue composables (`useXxx.ts`). Organized in subdirs for admin, space, widget.
  - **`hooks/`**: Runtime hooks (chat, session, msgInput, common, webRtc).
  - **`components/`**: Reusable Vue components (atomic, business, dm, room, thread, voice, widget, etc.).
  - **`workers/`**: Web Workers:
    - `matrixSdk.worker.ts` - Matrix SDK in dedicated thread (keep main thread < 50ms).
    - `fingerprint.worker.ts` - Device fingerprinting.
    - `imageDownloader.ts` - Background image downloads.
    - `timer.worker.ts` - Background timers.
  - **`utils/`**: Utilities (`Logger`, `HttpClient`, `MatrixUpload`, `RoomUtils`, `AudioManager`, `ImageUtils`, `LRUCache`, `TimerManager`, `PerformanceReporter`, `WebVitalsObserver`, etc.).
  - **`common/`**: Shared constants, error handling, result types, Matrix error translation.
  - **`types/`**: TypeScript type definitions including matrix-js-sdk augmentations.
  - **`strategy/`**: Message rendering strategy pattern (`MessageStrategy`, `strategies/`).
  - **`directives/`**: Custom Vue directives (`v-resize`, `v-slide`).
  - **`plugins/`**: Vue plugins (dynamic, i18n, robot).
  - **`layout/`**: App layout structures.
  - **`mobile/`**: Mobile-specific source overrides.
  - **`enums/`**: Shared enums.
  - **`styles/`**: SCSS styles; theme tokens in `src/styles/scss/global/variable.scss`.
- **`src-tauri/`**: Rust backend source code.
  - **`src/command/`**: Tauri command handlers: `admin_command`, `ai_command`, `app_state_command`, `chat_history_command`, `contact_command`, `database_command`, `file_manager_command`, `markdown_command`, `message_command`, `message_mark_command`, `oauth_command`, `room_member_command`, `setting_command`, `upload_command`, `user_command`.
  - **`src/repository/`**: Database repositories: `im_config`, `im_contact`, `im_message`, `im_room_member`, `im_user`.
  - **`src/common/`**: Shared utilities and helpers.
  - **`src/desktops/`**: Desktop-only code: `app_event`, `common_cmd`, `directory_scanner`, `init`, `tray`, `video_thumbnail`, `window_payload`.
  - **`src/mobiles/`**: Mobile-only code: `init`, `keyboard`, `splash`, iOS-specific.
  - **`entity/`**: SeaORM entity definitions (`im_config`, `im_contact`, `im_message`, `im_room`, `im_room_member`, `im_user`).
  - **`migration/`**: Database migration files.
  - **`tauri.conf.json`**: Base Tauri configuration; platform overrides: `tauri.windows.conf.json`, `tauri.macos.conf.json`, `tauri.linux.conf.json`, `tauri.android.conf.json`, `tauri.ios.conf.json`.
- **`tauri-plugin-hula/`**: Custom local Tauri plugin.
- **`vendor/matrix-js-sdk.tgz`**: Vendored Matrix SDK tarball (pinned via `meta/sdk-pin.json`; regenerate with `scripts/pack-sdk-tarball.mjs`).
- **`skills/hula-skill/`**: Custom development skill templates.
- **`build/`**: Vite build configuration helpers (`components.ts`, `chunks.ts`, `console.ts`).
- **`scripts/`**: Build and development helper scripts.

## Coding Style & Naming Conventions

- Indent 2 spaces, LF endings, trim trailing whitespace (see `.editorconfig`).
- Format/lint with Biome: `pnpm check` (read-only) / `pnpm check:write` (fixes). Vue templates use Prettier: `pnpm format:vue` or `pnpm format:all`.
- Import aliases: `@/` → `src/`, `#/` → `src/mobile/`, `~/` → repo root.
- Naming: components `PascalCase.vue`, composables `useXxx.ts`, Pinia stores in `src/stores/domains/`.
- **Commits:** Use `pnpm commit` to enforce Conventional Commits via Commitizen.
- **Styling:** Use UnoCSS utility classes; bracket syntax for CSS variables.
- **State:** Use Pinia for global state; prefer Composition API `<script setup>`.
- **Database:** Use SeaORM entities and repository layer for all DB access.
- **Services:** Matrix operations must go through service classes in `src/services/matrix/`; never call SDK directly from components or stores.
- **Tauri Commands:** Add new Rust commands in `src-tauri/src/command/` and register in `lib.rs`.

## Architecture Notes

### Three-Layer Architecture
TJG follows a three-layer architecture:
1. **Frontend Application** (Tauri + Vue 3 + TypeScript): Cross-platform desktop/mobile UI
2. **SDK Layer** (local matrix-js-sdk): Matrix protocol encapsulation, Sliding Sync, manager extensions
3. **Backend Service** (synapse-rust): Rust-based Matrix Homeserver

### 初始化与连接状态机（ADR-003）
- **永不白屏（乐观渲染）**：登录后立即用缓存数据渲染 UI，后台异步 `startClient()` + sync，成功后静默更新 store；失败显示连接状态横幅，仅在 access_token 401 且无缓存时才跳登录页。
- 连接状态机：`DISCONNECTED → CONNECTING → CONNECTED → SYNCING → CATCHUP → SYNCED`，任一环节可进入 `ERROR` 并自动指数退避重连。
- 单一数据源：统一用 Pinia store（持久化到 localStorage）；禁止 module-level ref；禁止 Web Worker 直接 fetch（一切 HTTP 走 SDK Manager）。
- 详见 `docs/adr/ADR-003-tjg-greenfield-rewrite.md`。

### Communication Patterns
- **Real-time Messaging:** Matrix Sliding Sync (frontend) / `tokio-tungstenite` WebSocket (Rust)
- **Frontend ↔ Rust:** Tauri commands (via `invoke`) defined in `src-tauri/src/command/`
- **Frontend ↔ Backend:** Matrix Client API through local matrix-js-sdk service layer
- **Heavy SDK work:** Offloaded to `matrixSdk.worker.ts` Web Worker; main thread stays responsive

### Key Architectural Patterns
- **Service Layer Pattern:** Matrix SDK wrapped in service classes organized by domain subdirectory
- **Repository Pattern:** Database access abstracted through repositories in `src-tauri/src/repository/`
- **Command Pattern:** Tauri commands expose Rust functionality to frontend
- **Strategy Pattern:** Message rendering via `src/strategy/MessageStrategy.ts`
- **Worker Pattern:** `matrixSdk.worker.ts` runs SDK in dedicated thread to prevent UI jank
- **Manager Extensions:** matrix-js-sdk includes custom manager extensions for synapse-rust specific features (imported via `’matrix-js-sdk/src/manager-extensions’`)

### Security
- **SQLite:** Local storage via `tauri-plugin-sql` + SeaORM; bundled `libsqlite3-sys`
- **Token Management:** Access tokens managed securely through Tauri backend
- **Error Handling:** `throwOnError` mode ensures all SDK errors surface and are logged

### Platform-Specific Code
- Desktop-only Rust code: `#[cfg(desktop)]`, lives in `src-tauri/src/desktops/`
- Mobile-only Rust code: `#[cfg(mobile)]`, lives in `src-tauri/src/mobiles/`
- Frontend platform detection: `TAURI_ENV_PLATFORM` env var; `~/` alias `#/` for mobile overrides
- Vite server ports: desktop `6130`, mobile `5210`
- Desktop UI: Naive UI; Mobile UI: Vant

## Security & Configuration

- Never add secrets or tokens to tracked files. Use `.env.local` for personal config.
- Key env vars: `VITE_HOMESERVER_URL` (Matrix homeserver), `VITE_APP_NAME`, `VITE_PC_URL`, `VITE_SERVICE_URL`.
- Package registry defaults to `.npmrc`; if unavailable override locally: `pnpm config set registry https://registry.npmjs.org/`.

## Important

- Do not prefix unused variables with an underscore, delete them instead
- Do not use emojis in commit messages, logs, or documentation
- Never change the .rules file unless the user specifically asks for it

## Pinia

This project uses Pinia for state management with specific patterns:

- Always create stores with the setup-style `defineStore(‘name’, () => { ... })` for better type safety and composition.
- Use `storeToRefs` when destructuring state so reactivity is preserved.
- Group business logic inside the store’s actions; components should only call actions/state.
- When a store depends on another store, import and call the other store factory inside the setup to share a single instance.
- Use `pinia-plugin-persistedstate` (already registered globally) for stores that must survive reloads—opt in per store via `persist: true`.
- Stores live under `src/stores/domains/` organized by domain: `chat/`, `settings/`, `user/`, `admin/`, `widget/`.

### Store Access Patterns

- Access other stores inside Pinia actions by instantiating the store at the top of the action: `const settings = useEditorSettingsStore();`
- Prefer reading dependent store state inside actions rather than passing parameters through components.
- Keep all imperative logic inside actions; components should remain declarative and simple.
- Avoid exporting raw refs outside of the store unless absolutely necessary; expose derived state through getters instead.

## CSS Variables & UnoCSS

Theme tokens live in `src/styles/scss/global/variable.scss`, but prefer inline UnoCSS utilities for simple light/dark styling.

**Defining Tokens**
- Default to per-element classes such as `bg-[lightColor] dark:bg-[darkColor]` or `text-[lightText] dark:text-[darkText]` so colors stay close to the component.
- Promote a color to `variable.scss` only when it is reused across multiple components or represents a semantic token (e.g. menu background).
- Keep light values on `:root` and dark overrides under `html[data-theme="dark"]` to leverage the existing data attribute toggle.
- When adding gradient or complex values, still store them as a variable (see `--bg-menu`) and document them inline in `variable.scss`.

**Using Tokens with UnoCSS**
- Prefer UnoCSS bracket syntax to consume tokens: `bg-[--center-bg-color]`, `text-[--text-color]`, `border-[--line-color]`.
- For multi-property helpers, apply directives are available because `@unocss/transformer-directives` is enabled: `@apply text-[--text-color]`.
- When a component needs conditional theming, toggle `data-theme` on `<html>` (light/dark) or add scoped data attributes (e.g. `data-theme="compact"`) and extend `variable.scss` with the selector.

## Language
- The language of the reply is determined based on the language of the user’s question. For example, if a user asks a question in simplified Chinese, reply in simplified Chinese.

## Working with Matrix SDK

### SDK Integration
- The project vendors a **local** matrix-js-sdk fork as a pinned tarball (`vendor/matrix-js-sdk.tgz`)
- Referenced via `"matrix-js-sdk": "file:vendor/matrix-js-sdk.tgz"` in package.json; `meta/sdk-pin.json` locks version/commit/SHA256
- Never modify SDK code directly; propose changes to the SDK repository instead
- SDK type augmentations live in `src/types/matrix-js-sdk-augmentations.d.ts`; verify with `pnpm check:sdk-types`

### Type Augmentations Maintenance
- **File**: `src/types/matrix-js-sdk-augmentations.d.ts` (1484 lines, 168 type definitions)
- **Purpose**: Extends matrix-js-sdk with missing type definitions
- **Structure**: Single file using `declare module` pattern (required by TypeScript)
- **Organization**: Divided into sections with `// ====` comments:
  - Basic types (Method, ClientPrefix, Visibility, etc.)
  - Interface supplements (ICreateRoomOpts, IPublicRoomsOpts, etc.)
  - OIDC types
  - Push notification types
  - Event and Timeline types
  - Voice/VoIP types
- **Important**: Do NOT split this file - TypeScript module augmentation requires all extensions in the same `declare module` block
- **Maintenance**: Add new types in the appropriate section, keep comments updated

### Service Layer Pattern
- All Matrix SDK calls must go through service classes in `src/services/matrix/`
- Services are organized by subdomain: `auth/`, `room/`, `messaging/`, `media/`, `user/`, `friends/`, `notifications/`, `crypto/`, `sync/`, `admin/`, `ai/`, `widget/`
- Components should never import or call matrix-js-sdk directly
- `MatrixClientService` manages the underlying `MatrixClient` instance and Sliding Sync initialization

### Sliding Sync
- TJG uses Sliding Sync (`SlidingSync`) for efficient, incremental room list sync
- Managed by `MatrixSlidingSyncService` and `SlidingSyncReconnectManager`
- The `MatrixClientService` initializes `SlidingSync` on startup

### Web Worker
- Matrix SDK heavy operations run in `src/workers/matrixSdk.worker.ts`
- Communicate via typed message passing (`WorkerMessage` / `WorkerResponse`)
- Keep main thread blocking time < 50ms

### Error Handling
- SDK uses `throwOnError` mode: read operations throw exceptions by default
- Always wrap SDK calls in try-catch blocks within service methods
- Log errors using `@tauri-apps/plugin-log` (`info`, `error`, `warn` functions)
- Translate SDK errors to user-friendly messages via `src/common/matrixErrorTranslator.ts`

### API Contract
- Follow the matrix-js-sdk API contract for all SDK interactions
- Respect the contract’s error handling patterns and return types
- When adding new SDK features, ensure they follow the established contract patterns

## AI Integration

TJG integrates multiple AI providers via `src/services/ai-provider.ts`:
- **OpenClaw** (`src/services/openclaw/`): OpenAI-compatible gateway with streaming and auto-reconnect
- **SiliconFlow** (`src/services/siliconflow/`): SiliconFlow AI provider
- **TrendRadar** (`src/services/trendradar/`): Trending news and content aggregation
- **Matrix AI** (`src/services/matrix/ai/`): AI features via Matrix protocol (conversations, models, roles, API keys)

AI provider config is unified under `AIProviderType = ‘openclaw’ | ‘trendradar’ | ‘hula’`. The AI chat UI lives in `src/views/openclaw/OpenClawView.vue`.

## Skill routing

当用户请求匹配某个技能时，先通过 Skill 工具调用，再谈实现。

关键路由规则：
- 任何重构/新功能动手前 → writing-plans（先写方案）
- 设计取舍/范围收敛 → brainstorming / grilling
- 写实现代码前 → test-driven-development（先写失败测试）
- 执行多任务计划 → subagent-driven-development 或 executing-plans
- 声称"完成/修复/通过"前 → verification-before-completion（先跑命令取证）
- 收到评审反馈 → receiving-code-review（先核实再采纳，不盲从）
- 请人评审 → requesting-code-review（见下方质量门禁）
- 需要隔离工作区 → using-git-worktrees
- 出现 bug → systematic-debugging（先诊断再修）

## UI 设计系统强制规范

- 设计 token 唯一来源：`src/styles/css/design-tokens.css`（权威），`variable.scss` 仅作旧别名层。
- 禁止硬编码颜色：新代码一律使用 `--tjg-*` token；不得出现 `#xxx`/`rgb()`/`rgba()` 新增值。
- 图标必须使用 SVG：禁止 div-based 图标；图标用 `<svg>` / `<use>` / Iconify，线宽 1.5px。
- 组件体量红线：任何 `.vue` 文件超过 800 行必须拆分（参照 workbench 层样板）。
- 桌面/移动端策略：优先补全 `src/mobile/` 独立实现；`isMobile()` 内联分支只允许在临界候补组件，禁止新增。
- 动效必须尊重 `prefers-reduced-motion`。
- 语义色/状态色用 token（`--tjg-status-*`），不依赖颜色传达状态。

## 重构验收命令

每次改动后必须跑以下守门命令：

| 命令 | 用途 |
| :--- | :--- |
| `pnpm vue-tsc --noEmit` | 类型检查，必须 0 错误 |
| `pnpm test:run` | 单元测试全部通过 |
| `pnpm check:ratchet` | 硬编码颜色/样式守护（ratchet） |
| `pnpm check:doc-coverage` | 文档覆盖守护 |
| `pnpm check:sdk-boundary` | SDK 边界守护 |
| `pnpm quality:no-raw-fetch` | 禁止直接 fetch 守护 |
| `pnpm check` | Biome lint + i18n 检查 |
| `pnpm storybook` | 视觉回归（可选，涉及组件时） |
